[TestRuleVMAlertLimit/recording_rule_returning_more_series_than_the_group_limit - 1]
- description: recording rule returning more series than the group limit
  content: |
    - name: g
      limit: 2
      rules:
      - record: foo:sum
        expr: sum(foo) by (instance)
  output: |
    5 |     expr: sum(foo) by (instance)
                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                  `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com returned 10 result(s) for this
                  query, more than `limit: 2` of the group: vmalert would fail this rule with `exec exceeded
                  limit of 2 with 10 series` and drop all its results.
  problem:
    reporter: rule/vmalert
    summary: rule returns more results than vmalert allows
    details: 'vmalert fails a rule that returns more results than `limit` of its group, or `-rule.resultsLimit` when the group doesn''t set one: the rule is marked with an error and all its results are dropped, so a recording rule writes nothing and an alerting rule fires nothing. Make the query return fewer series, or raise the limit. See [vmalert groups](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/vmalert/#groups).'
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com returned 10 result(s) for this query, more than `limit: 2` of the group: vmalert would fail this rule with `exec exceeded limit of 2 with 10 series` and drop all its results.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 22
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 5
        last: 5
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

---

[TestRuleVMAlertLimit/alerting_rule_returning_more_alerts_than_the_group_limit - 1]
- description: alerting rule returning more alerts than the group limit
  content: |
    - name: g
      limit: 2
      rules:
      - alert: FooHigh
        expr: foo > 1
  output: |
    5 |     expr: foo > 1
                  ^^^^^^^
                  `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com returned 3 result(s) for this
                  query, more than `limit: 2` of the group: vmalert would fail this rule with `exec exceeded
                  limit of 2 with 3 alerts` and drop all its results.
  problem:
    reporter: rule/vmalert
    summary: rule returns more results than vmalert allows
    details: 'vmalert fails a rule that returns more results than `limit` of its group, or `-rule.resultsLimit` when the group doesn''t set one: the rule is marked with an error and all its results are dropped, so a recording rule writes nothing and an alerting rule fires nothing. Make the query return fewer series, or raise the limit. See [vmalert groups](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/vmalert/#groups).'
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com returned 3 result(s) for this query, more than `limit: 2` of the group: vmalert would fail this rule with `exec exceeded limit of 2 with 3 alerts` and drop all its results.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 7
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 5
        last: 5
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

