[TestRuleVMAlertDuplicateGroupName/the_same_group_name_twice_in_one_data_key - 1]
- description: the same group name twice in one data key
  content: |
    apiVersion: v1
    kind: ConfigMap
    metadata:
      name: rules
    data:
      a.yaml: |
        groups:
          - name: same
            rules: []
          - name: same
            rules:
              - record: r:sum
                expr: sum(up)
  output: |
    10 |       - name: same
                       ^^^^
                       Another group in this file is also named `same`: vmalert fails to load the whole file
                       with `group name "same" duplicate in file`.
  problem:
    reporter: rule/vmalert
    summary: duplicated group name
    details: vmalert refuses to load a rule file with two groups of the same name, so none of the rules in that file are evaluated. Group names must be unique within a file. In a ConfigMap every data key is a separate file, and so is the spec of a VMRule.
    diagnostics:
        - message: 'Another group in this file is also named `same`: vmalert fails to load the whole file with `group name "same" duplicate in file`.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 4
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 10
        last: 10
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

